<title>USA: Reeds Jewelers Q2 EPS falls to $0.05.</title>
<headline>Reeds Jewelers Q2 EPS falls to $0.05.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, N.C. 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>			  8/31/96		     8/31/95</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.05		    $0.11</p>
<p> Net			  205.0		   444.0</p>
<p> Revs		    20,168.0		 16,185.0</p>
<p> Avg shrs	     4,222,061		4,201,281</p>
<p>	    6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.10		    $0.20</p>
<p> Net			  441.0		    826.0</p>
<p> Revs		    40,869.0		33,330.0</p>
<p> Avg shrs	     4,219,249		4,201,281</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers) NOTE: Alan  M. Zimmer, president and chief executive officer, said in a statement: &quot;While both the Melart and Reeds stores posted strong sales results, our earnings for the quarter were impacted by the higher operating costs associated with the Melart stores. Since acquiring Melart last October, we have been working hard to bring their operating costs in line with those of our core store base and saw significant improvements this quarter.&quot;</p>
</text>
